  "summary": "“Carlisle.”\nCharlie paused, his hand still frozen behind his head. He raised a brow, his mind taking a second to process the single, offered word through the haze of his embarrassment.\n“Huh?”\nA patient, understanding smile touched the doctor’s lips\n“Call me Carlisle.”\n“Carlisle,” Charlie repeated, testing the name himself. It sounded gritty and rough on his tongue, a common stone compared to the polished gem of the doctor’s pronunciation.\nHe couldn’t make it sound pretty.\nHe could only make it sound real.\n-----------------\nOr, a retelling of the first Twilight book revolving around Charlie and Carlisle’s budding relationship. (Will mostly follow through the first half of the book and then diverge from canon as their relationship grows)",
